{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 60,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- This is a video about\none of the most important,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2850,
    "dDurationMs": 4260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "yet least understood\nconcepts in all of physics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 7110,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It governs everything\nfrom molecular collisions"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 9990,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to humongous storms."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12330,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "From the beginning of the universe"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 14850,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "through its entire evolution,\nto its inevitable end."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 19650,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It may, in fact, determine\nthe direction of time"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 22290,
    "dDurationMs": 3150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and even be the reason that life exists."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 25440,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To see the confusion around this topic,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 27960,
    "dDurationMs": 2943,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you need to ask only one simple question."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 31800,
    "dDurationMs": 2643,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What does the Earth get from the sun?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 35400,
    "dDurationMs": 1750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- What does the earth get from sun?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 39390,
    "dDurationMs": 1650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Well, it's light rays?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41040,
    "dDurationMs": 2019,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- What do we get from the sun?\n- Heat."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 43059,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Warmth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 43892,
    "dDurationMs": 2008,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Warmth, light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45900,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Vitamin D, we get vitamin D from-"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 47400,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- We do get vitamin D\nfrom the ultraviolet rays."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 49350,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Well, a lot of energy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 51450,
    "dDurationMs": 1780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- What does the earth\nget from this, energy?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 53230,
    "dDurationMs": 1490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Yeah, energy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 54720,
    "dDurationMs": 1620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Energy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 56340,
    "dDurationMs": 1110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Nailed it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 57450,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Every day, the earth gets\na certain amount of energy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 59490,
    "dDurationMs": 1290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from the sun."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 60780,
    "dDurationMs": 4050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And then how much energy\ndoes the earth radiate back"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 64830,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "into space relative to that amount"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 66630,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that it gets from the sun?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 67830,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Probably not as much, I, you know,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 69630,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I don't believe it's just\nradiating right back."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 72570,
    "dDurationMs": 1467,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- I'd say less."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 74037,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Less."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 74870,
    "dDurationMs": 1196,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Less.\n- I say less."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 76066,
    "dDurationMs": 1194,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- I guess about 70%?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 77260,
    "dDurationMs": 1250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- It is a fraction."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78510,
    "dDurationMs": 1033,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- I'd say 20%."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 79543,
    "dDurationMs": 2537,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Because...\n- Because we use some of it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 82080,
    "dDurationMs": 1170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- We use some of the energy.\n- Mm-hmm."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 83250,
    "dDurationMs": 1620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- We consume a lot, right?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 84870,
    "dDurationMs": 3180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- But the thing about energy\nis it never really goes away."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 88050,
    "dDurationMs": 1473,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can't really use it up."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 90420,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- It would have to\nbreak even, wouldn't it?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92580,
    "dDurationMs": 1050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Same amount, yeah."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 93630,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- You know, cause and effect."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 95310,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It'd be equal in some ways, right?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 97530,
    "dDurationMs": 1650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- For most of the earth's history,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 99180,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it should be exactly the\nsame amount of energy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 101550,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in from the sun as earth\nradiates into space."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 105270,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Wow."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 106103,
    "dDurationMs": 1927,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Because if we didn't do that,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 108030,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then the earth would get a lot\nhotter, that'd be a problem."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 110190,
    "dDurationMs": 1050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- That'd be a big problem."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 111240,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So, if that is the case..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 113280,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Yeah."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 114113,
    "dDurationMs": 2027,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Then what are we really\ngetting from the sun?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 117900,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- That's a good question."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 118733,
    "dDurationMs": 1177,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Hmm."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 119910,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- It gives us a nice tan."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 121650,
    "dDurationMs": 1770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- It gives us a nice tan, I love it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 123420,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We're getting something\nspecial from the sun."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 125280,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- I don't know, what do\nwe get without the energy?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 127770,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- But nobody talks about it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 129600,
    "dDurationMs": 2730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To answer that, we have\nto go back to a discovery"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 132330,
    "dDurationMs": 2073,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "made two centuries ago."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 135720,
    "dDurationMs": 2910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the winter of 1813,\nFrance was being invaded"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 138630,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by the armies of Austria,\nPrussia, and Russia."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 142110,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The son of one of Napoleon's generals"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 144060,
    "dDurationMs": 3390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was Sadi Carnot, a 17-year-old student."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 147450,
    "dDurationMs": 2730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "On December 29th, he\nwrites a letter to Napoleon"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 150180,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to request to join in the fight."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 152610,
    "dDurationMs": 4260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Napoleon preoccupied in\nbattle, never replies."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 156870,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but Carnot gets his\nwish a few months later"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 159150,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when Paris is attacked."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 161070,
    "dDurationMs": 3450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The students defend a chateau\njust east of the city,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 164520,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but there're no match\nfor the advancing armies,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 167340,
    "dDurationMs": 3390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and Paris falls after\nonly a day of fighting."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 170730,
    "dDurationMs": 3243,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Forced to retreat, Carnot is devastated."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 176280,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Seven years later, he\ngoes to visit his father"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 179040,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "who's fled to Prussia\nafter Napoleon's downfall."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 182400,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "His father was not only a\ngeneral, but also a physicist."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 186120,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He wrote an essay on how energy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 187800,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is most efficiently transferred\nin mechanical systems."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 191640,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When his son comes to\nvisit, they talk at length"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 194310,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "about the big breakthrough\nof the time, steam engines."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 198390,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Steam engines were already\nbeing used to power ships,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 201330,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "mine ore, and excavate ports."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 204330,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And it was clear that\nthe future industrial"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 206610,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and military might of nations"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 208740,
    "dDurationMs": 3333,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "depended on having the best steam engines."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 213150,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But French designs were falling behind"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 215220,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "those of other countries like Britain."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 217590,
    "dDurationMs": 4113,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, Sadi Carnot took it upon\nhimself to figure out why."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 225480,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At the time, even the best steam engines"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 227400,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "only converted around 3% of thermal energy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 230100,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "into useful mechanical work."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 232590,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If he could improve on\nthat, he could give France"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 235380,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a huge advantage and restore\nits place in the world."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 239700,
    "dDurationMs": 3930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So he spends the next three\nyears studying heat engines,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 243630,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and one of his key insights"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 245610,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "involves how an ideal\nheat engine would work,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 248850,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "one with no friction and no\nlosses to the environment."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 252690,
    "dDurationMs": 2253,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It looks something like this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 256410,
    "dDurationMs": 4380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Take two really big metal\nbars, one hot and one cold."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 260790,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The engine consists of a\nchamber filled with air,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 264270,
    "dDurationMs": 3810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where heat can only flow in\nor out through the bottom."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 268080,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Inside the chamber is a piston,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 270060,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is connected to a flywheel."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 272460,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The air starts at a\ntemperature just below that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 275220,
    "dDurationMs": 1350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the hot bar."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 276570,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So first, the hot bar\nis brought into contact"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 278820,
    "dDurationMs": 840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with the chamber."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 279660,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The air inside expands\nwith heat flowing into it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 282960,
    "dDurationMs": 1650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to maintain its temperature."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 284610,
    "dDurationMs": 3750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This pushes the piston\nup, turning the flywheel."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 288360,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Next, the hot bar is removed,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 290250,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but the air in the chamber\ncontinues to expand,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 293550,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "except now without heat entering,\nthe temperature decreases."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 297870,
    "dDurationMs": 1020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the ideal case,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 298890,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "until it is the temperature\nof the cold bar."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 301830,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The cold bar is brought into\ncontact with the chamber"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 304080,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the flywheel pushes the piston down."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 306690,
    "dDurationMs": 1470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And as the air is compressed,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 308160,
    "dDurationMs": 3210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "heat is transferred into the cold bar."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 311370,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The cold bar is removed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 312930,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The flywheel compresses the gas further"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 315240,
    "dDurationMs": 2510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "increasing its temperature\nuntil it is just below that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 317750,
    "dDurationMs": 1480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the hot bar."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 319230,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then the hot bar is connected\nagain and the cycle repeats."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 323190,
    "dDurationMs": 3750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Through this process, heat\nfrom the hot bar is converted"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 326940,
    "dDurationMs": 2283,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "into the energy of the flywheel."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 330060,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And what's interesting to note\nabout Carnot's ideal engine"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 333150,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is that it is completely reversible."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 335940,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you ran the engine in reverse,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 338400,
    "dDurationMs": 3450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "first the air expands\nlowering the temperature,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 341850,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then the chamber is brought\ninto contact with the cold bar,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 344850,
    "dDurationMs": 4020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the air expands more, drawing\nin heat from the cold bar."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 348870,
    "dDurationMs": 3810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Next, the air is compressed,\nincreasing its temperature."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 352680,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The chamber is placed\non top of the hot bar"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 354720,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the energy of the flywheel\nis used to return the heat"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 358140,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "back into the hot bar."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 360660,
    "dDurationMs": 3150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "However many cycles were run\nin the forward direction,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 363810,
    "dDurationMs": 3660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you could run the same number\nin reverse, and at the end,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 367470,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "everything would return\nto its original state"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 370140,
    "dDurationMs": 3870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with no additional input\nof energy required."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 374010,
    "dDurationMs": 3810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So by running an ideal engine,\nnothing really changes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 377820,
    "dDurationMs": 2403,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can always undo what you did."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 382080,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what is the efficiency of this engine?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 385140,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Since it's fully reversible,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 386970,
    "dDurationMs": 3270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you might expect the\nefficiency to be 100%,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 390240,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but that is not the case."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 392520,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Each cycle, the energy\nof the flywheel increases"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 395190,
    "dDurationMs": 1260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by the amount of heat flowing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 396450,
    "dDurationMs": 2190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "into the chamber from the hot bar,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 398640,
    "dDurationMs": 4140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "minus the heat flowing out of\nthe chamber at the cold bar."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 402780,
    "dDurationMs": 3390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So to calculate the efficiency,\nwe divide this energy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 406170,
    "dDurationMs": 2493,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by the heat input from the hot bar."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 410010,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now the heat in on the hot\nside is equal to the work done"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 413310,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by the gas on the piston,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 415470,
    "dDurationMs": 2730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and this will always be\ngreater than the work done"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 418200,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by the piston on the gas on the cold side,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 421140,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which equals the heat out."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 423390,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this is because on the hot side,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 425220,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the hot gas exerts a greater pressure"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 427680,
    "dDurationMs": 3930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on the piston than that\nsame gas when cold."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 431610,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To increase the efficiency of the engine,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 433650,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you could increase the\ntemperature of the hot side,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 436350,
    "dDurationMs": 3543,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or decrease the temperature\nof the cold side, or both."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 441870,
    "dDurationMs": 2910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Lord Kelvin learns of\nCarnot's ideal heat engine"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 444780,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and realizes it could form the basis"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 447540,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for an absolute temperature scale."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 450150,
    "dDurationMs": 4050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Imagine that the gas is allowed\nto expand an extreme amount,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 454200,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so much that it cools to the point"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 456090,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where all the gas particles\neffectively stop moving."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 459630,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then they would exert no\npressure on the piston,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 462690,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it would take no work to compress it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 464940,
    "dDurationMs": 3870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on the cold side, so\nno heat would be lost."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 468810,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is the idea of absolute zero,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 472230,
    "dDurationMs": 3990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it would make for a\n100% efficient engine."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 476220,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Using this absolute temperature\nscale, the Kelvin scale,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 480060,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we can replace the\namount of heat in and out"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 482880,
    "dDurationMs": 3630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with the temperature of the\nhot and cold side respectively,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 486510,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because they are directly proportional."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 489180,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So we can express efficiency like this,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 491640,
    "dDurationMs": 2373,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which we can rewrite like this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 495420,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What we have learned\nis that the efficiency"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 497160,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of an ideal heat engine\ndoesn't depend on the materials"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 500100,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or the design of the engine,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 501930,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but fundamentally on the temperatures"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 503850,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the hot and cold sides."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 506280,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To reach 100% efficiency,\nyou'd need infinite temperature"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 509250,
    "dDurationMs": 3150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on the hot side or absolute\nzero on the cold side,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 512400,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "both of which are impossible in practice."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 515190,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So even with no friction or\nlosses to the environment,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 517800,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's impossible to make a\nheat engine 100% efficient."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 521520,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that's because to return the piston"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 523350,
    "dDurationMs": 1350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to its original position,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 524700,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you need to dump heat into the cold bar."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 527280,
    "dDurationMs": 3153,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So not all the energy\nstays in the flywheel."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 531660,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, in Carnot's time,\nhigh pressure steam engines"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 534300,
    "dDurationMs": 3510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "could only reach temperatures\nup to 160 degrees Celsius."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 537810,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So their theoretical\nmaximum efficiency was 32%,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 542010,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but their real efficiency\nwas more like 3%."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 545430,
    "dDurationMs": 2910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's because real engines\nexperience friction,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 548340,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "dissipate heat to the environment,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 550080,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they don't transfer heat\nat constant temperatures."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 553380,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So for just as much heat going in,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 555750,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "less energy ends up in the flywheel."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 558540,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The rest is spread out over\nthe walls of the cylinder,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 561540,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the axle of the flywheel,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 563280,
    "dDurationMs": 3510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and is radiated out into the environment."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 566790,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When energy spreads out like this,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 569010,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it is impossible to get it back."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 571380,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So this process is irreversible."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 574380,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The total amount of energy didn't change,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 577020,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but it became less usable."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 579600,
    "dDurationMs": 3660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Energy is most usable\nwhen it is concentrated"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 583260,
    "dDurationMs": 2313,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and less usable when it's spread out."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 588540,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Decades later, German\nphysicist, Rudolf Clausius,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 591540,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "studies Carnot's engine,\nand he comes up with a way"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 594510,
    "dDurationMs": 3660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to measure how spread out the energy is."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 598170,
    "dDurationMs": 2793,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He calls this quantity, entropy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 602160,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When all the energy is\nconcentrated in the hot bar,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 605160,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that is low entropy,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 607590,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but as the energy spreads\nto the surroundings,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 610380,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the walls of the chamber and the axle"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 612690,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "will entropy increases."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 615030,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This means the same amount\nof energy is present,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 617910,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but in this more dispersed form,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 619770,
    "dDurationMs": 2403,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it is less available to do work."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 623430,
    "dDurationMs": 3690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In 1865, Clausius summarizes\nthe first two laws"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 627120,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of thermodynamics like this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 629520,
    "dDurationMs": 3690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "First, the energy of the\nuniverse is constant."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 633210,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And second, the entropy of the\nuniverse tends to a maximum."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 638970,
    "dDurationMs": 3573,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In other words, energy\nspreads out over time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 644910,
    "dDurationMs": 3390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The second law is core to so\nmany phenomena in the world."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 648300,
    "dDurationMs": 3510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's why hot things cool\ndown and cool things heat up,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 651810,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "why gas expands to fill a container,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 654180,
    "dDurationMs": 2910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "why you can't have a\nperpetual motion machine,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 657090,
    "dDurationMs": 3180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because the amount of usable\nenergy in a closed system"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 660270,
    "dDurationMs": 1683,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is always decreasing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 664050,
    "dDurationMs": 4050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The most common way to describe\nentropy is as disorder,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 668100,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which makes sense because\nit is associated with things"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 670860,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "becoming more mixed,\nrandom, and less ordered."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 674160,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But I think the best way\nto think about entropy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 676080,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is as the tendency of\nenergy to spread out."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 679560,
    "dDurationMs": 3030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So why does energy spread out over time?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 682590,
    "dDurationMs": 1410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean, most of the laws of physics"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 684000,
    "dDurationMs": 4050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "work exactly the same way\nforwards or backwards in time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 688050,
    "dDurationMs": 3963,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So how does this clear\ntime dependence arise?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 694530,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, let's consider two small metal bars,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 696930,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "one hot and one cold."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 698910,
    "dDurationMs": 1260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For this simple model,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 700170,
    "dDurationMs": 3210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we'll consider only eight atoms per bar."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 703380,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Each atom vibrates according to the number"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 705180,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of energy packets it has."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 706860,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The more packets, the more it vibrates."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 709230,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So let's start with\nseven packets of energy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 711300,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the left bar and three in the right."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 714120,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The number of energy packets in each bar"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 715920,
    "dDurationMs": 1923,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is what we'll call a state."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 718890,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "First, let's consider just the left bar."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 721320,
    "dDurationMs": 1620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It has seven energy packets,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 722940,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which are free to move around the lattice."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 725220,
    "dDurationMs": 1530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This happens nonstop."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 726750,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The energy packets hop\nrandomly from atom to atom"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 729630,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "giving different configurations of energy,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 732240,
    "dDurationMs": 3990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but the total energy stays\nthe same the whole time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 736230,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, let's bring the cold bar back in"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 738180,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with only three packets\nand touch them together."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 741270,
    "dDurationMs": 1710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The energy packets can now hop around"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 742980,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "between both bars creating\ndifferent configurations."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 746520,
    "dDurationMs": 3510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Each unique configuration\nis equally likely."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 750030,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what happens if we take a\nsnapshot at one instant in time"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 753570,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and see where all the energy packets are?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 756030,
    "dDurationMs": 3660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So stop, look at this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 759690,
    "dDurationMs": 3330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now there are nine energy\npackets in the left bar,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 763020,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and only one in the right bar."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 765420,
    "dDurationMs": 3630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So heat has flowed from cold to hot."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 769050,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Shouldn't that be impossible\nbecause it decreases entropy?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 773730,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, this is where Ludwig Boltzmann"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 775830,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "made an important insight."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 777630,
    "dDurationMs": 4230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Heat flowing from cold\nto hot is not impossible,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 781860,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's just improbable."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 784290,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There are 91,520 configurations"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 787650,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with nine energy packets in the left bar,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 790410,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but 627,264 with five\nenergy packets in each bar."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 796800,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is the energy is more than six times"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 799380,
    "dDurationMs": 3180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as likely to be evenly\nspread between the bars."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 802560,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if you add up all the possibilities,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 804810,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you find there's still a\n10.5% chance that the left bar"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 808770,
    "dDurationMs": 2913,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ends up with more energy\npackets than it started."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 812580,
    "dDurationMs": 3690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, why don't we observe\nthis happening around us?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 816270,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, watch what happens as we\nincrease the number of atoms"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 818940,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to 80 per bar and the\nenergy packets to 100,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 822180,
    "dDurationMs": 3630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with 70 in the left bar\nand 30 in the right."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 825810,
    "dDurationMs": 4050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There is now only a 0.05%\nchance that the left solid"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 829860,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ends up hotter than it started."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 832290,
    "dDurationMs": 3660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this trend continues as\nwe keep scaling up the system."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 835950,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In everyday solids, there\nare around 100 trillion,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 839190,
    "dDurationMs": 3510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "trillion atoms and even\nmore energy packets."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 842700,
    "dDurationMs": 4230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So heat flowing from cold\nto hot is just so unlikely"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 846930,
    "dDurationMs": 1443,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that it never happens."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 850290,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Think of it like this Rubik's cube."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 852390,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Right now, it is completely solved,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 854670,
    "dDurationMs": 4170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but I'm gonna close my eyes\nand make some turns at random."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 858840,
    "dDurationMs": 2730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If I keep doing this, it\nwill get further and further"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 861570,
    "dDurationMs": 1410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from being solved."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 862980,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But how can I be confident\nthat I'm really messing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 866070,
    "dDurationMs": 1320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this cube up?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 867390,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, because there's only\none way for it to be solved,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 870000,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a few ways for it to be almost solved,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 872280,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and quintillions of ways"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 874350,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for it to be almost entirely random."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 876930,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Without thought and effort,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 878610,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "every turn moves the Rubik's cube"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 880590,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from a highly unlikely state\nthat of it being solved"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 883890,
    "dDurationMs": 3333,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to a more likely state, a total mess."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 890220,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if the natural tendency\nof energy is to spread out"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 893010,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and for things to get messier,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 895110,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then how is it possible to have something"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 897210,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like air conditioning where\nthe cold interior of a house"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 901410,
    "dDurationMs": 3363,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "gets cooler and the hot\nexterior gets hotter?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 906060,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Energy is going from cold to hot,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 908850,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "decreasing the entropy of the house."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 912090,
    "dDurationMs": 4050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, this decrease in\nentropy is only possible"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 916140,
    "dDurationMs": 4170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by increasing the entropy a\ngreater amount somewhere else."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 920310,
    "dDurationMs": 1620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In this case, at a power plant,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 921930,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the concentrated chemical energy\nand coal is being released,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 926130,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "heating up the power\nplant in its environment,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 928770,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "spreading to the turbine\nthe electric generators,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 931770,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "heating the wires all\nthe way to the house,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 933900,
    "dDurationMs": 3570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and producing waste heat\nin the fans and compressor."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 937470,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Whatever decrease in entropy\nis achieved at the house"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 940950,
    "dDurationMs": 3930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is more than paid for by an\nincrease in entropy required"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 944880,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to make that happen."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 947670,
    "dDurationMs": 3030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if total entropy is\nconstantly increasing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 950700,
    "dDurationMs": 3630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and anything we do only\naccelerates that increase,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 954330,
    "dDurationMs": 3810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then how is there any\nstructure left on earth?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 958140,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "How are there hot parts\nseparate from cold parts?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 961680,
    "dDurationMs": 2013,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "How does life exist?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 965010,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, if the earth were a closed system,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 967110,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the energy would spread out completely,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 969720,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "meaning, all life would cease,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 972120,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "everything would decay and mix,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 974520,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and eventually, reach\nthe same temperature."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 977760,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But luckily, earth is not a closed system,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 981540,
    "dDurationMs": 3231,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because we have the sun."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 988350,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What the sun really gives\nus is a steady stream"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 991170,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of low entropy that is\nconcentrated bundled up energy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 995970,
    "dDurationMs": 3690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The energy that we get\nfrom the sun is more useful"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 999660,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "than the energy we give back."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1001100,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's more compact, it's\nmore clumped together."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1004220,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Plants capture this\nenergy and use it to grow"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1006980,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and create sugars."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1008720,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then animals eat plants\nand use that energy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1011420,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to maintain their bodies and move around."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1014240,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Bigger animals get their energy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1015800,
    "dDurationMs": 3030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by eating smaller animals and so on."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1018830,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And each step of the way,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1020690,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the energy becomes more spread out."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1023240,
    "dDurationMs": 990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Okay, interesting."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1024230,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Yeah."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1025063,
    "dDurationMs": 1897,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Oh wow, I did not know that."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1026960,
    "dDurationMs": 1110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- There you go."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1028070,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ultimately, all the energy\nthat reaches earth from the sun"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1031430,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is converted into thermal energy,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1033950,
    "dDurationMs": 3330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then it's radiated back into space."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1037280,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But in fact, it's the same amount."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1039680,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I know this is a-\n- You do know this is..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1041780,
    "dDurationMs": 1334,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- I'm a PhD physicist."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1043114,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Oh, okay, but anyway, so...\n- I trust you."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1047660,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The increase in entropy can be seen"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1049820,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the relative number\nof photons arriving at"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1052460,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and leaving the earth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1054770,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For each photon received from the sun,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1058070,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "20 photons are emitted,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1060650,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and everything that happens on earth,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1062960,
    "dDurationMs": 4020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "plants growing, trees\nfalling, herds stampeding,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1066980,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hurricanes and tornadoes, people eating,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1069830,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sleeping, and breathing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1071330,
    "dDurationMs": 4110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All of it happens in the\nprocess of converting fewer,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1075440,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "higher energy photons"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1077000,
    "dDurationMs": 4050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "into 20 times as many\nlower energy photons."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1081050,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Without a source of concentrated energy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1083420,
    "dDurationMs": 3450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and a way to discard\nthe spread out energy,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1086870,
    "dDurationMs": 3450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "life on earth would not be possible."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1090320,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It has even been\nsuggested that life itself"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1092660,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "may be a consequence of the\nsecond law of thermodynamics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1096200,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If the universe tends\ntoward maximum entropy,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1099020,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then life offers a way to\naccelerate that natural tendency,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1103520,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because life is spectacularly good"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1106280,
    "dDurationMs": 3690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at converting low entropy\ninto high entropy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1109970,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, the surface\nlayer of seawater produces"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1112850,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "between 30 to 680% more\nentropy when cyanobacteria"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1118970,
    "dDurationMs": 3810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and other organic matter is\npresent than when it's not."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1122780,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Jeremy England takes\nthis one step further."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1125360,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He's proposed that if\nthere is a constant stream"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1128030,
    "dDurationMs": 3180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of clumped up energy, this\ncould favor structures"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1131210,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that dissipate that energy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1133460,
    "dDurationMs": 1710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And over time, this results"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1135170,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in better and better energy dissipators,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1137540,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "eventually resulting in life."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1140120,
    "dDurationMs": 1207,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or in his own words,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1141327,
    "dDurationMs": 2663,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"You start with a random clump of atoms,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1143990,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and if you shine light\non it for long enough,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1146420,
    "dDurationMs": 3447,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it should not be so surprising\nthat you get a plant.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1151190,
    "dDurationMs": 4230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So life on earth survives on\nthe low entropy from the sun,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1155420,
    "dDurationMs": 3990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but then where did the\nsun get its low entropy?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1159410,
    "dDurationMs": 3180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The answer is the universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1162590,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If we know that the total\nentropy of the universe"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1165020,
    "dDurationMs": 4530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is increasing with time, then\nit was lower entropy yesterday"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1169550,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and even lower entropy\nthe day before that,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1171920,
    "dDurationMs": 2793,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and so on, all the way\nback to the Big Bang."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1177110,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So right after the Big Bang,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1178970,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that is when the entropy was lowest."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1181730,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is known as the past hypothesis."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1184700,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It doesn't explain why\nthe entropy was low,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1187250,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just that it must have been\nthat way for the universe"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1189290,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to unfold as it has."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1191840,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the early universe was hot, dense,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1194720,
    "dDurationMs": 2190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and almost completely uniform."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1196910,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean, everything was\nmixed and the temperature"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1199220,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was basically the same everywhere,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1201500,
    "dDurationMs": 4380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "varying by at most 0.001%."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1205880,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So how is this low entropy?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1209000,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, the thing we've left out is gravity."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1211850,
    "dDurationMs": 3150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Gravity tends to clump matter together."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1215000,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So taking gravity into account,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1216830,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "having matter all spread out like this,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1219230,
    "dDurationMs": 2730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "would be an extremely unlikely state,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1221960,
    "dDurationMs": 2703,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that is why it's low entropy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1226520,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Over time, as the universe\nexpanded and cooled,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1229610,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "matter started to clump\ntogether in more dense regions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1233150,
    "dDurationMs": 3390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And in doing so, enormous\namounts of potential energy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1236540,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "were turned into kinetic energy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1238220,
    "dDurationMs": 3390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this energy could also be used"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1241610,
    "dDurationMs": 3033,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like how water flowing\ndownhill can power a turbine."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1245480,
    "dDurationMs": 3030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But as bits of matter\nstarted hitting each other,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1248510,
    "dDurationMs": 3030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "some of their kinetic energy\nwas converted into heat."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1251540,
    "dDurationMs": 3630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the amount of useful energy decreased."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1255170,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Thereby, increasing entropy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1258050,
    "dDurationMs": 3570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Over time, the useful energy was used."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1261620,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In doing so, stars, planets,\ngalaxies, and life were formed,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1266300,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "increasing entropy all along."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1269180,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The universe started with around 10"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1271340,
    "dDurationMs": 3750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the 88 Boltzmann\nconstants worth of entropy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1275090,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Nowadays, all the stars\nin the observable universe"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1277700,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have about 9.5 times 10 to the 80."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1280790,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The interstellar and\nintergalactic medium combined"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1283550,
    "dDurationMs": 2190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have almost 10 times more,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1285740,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but still only a fraction\nof the early universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1289640,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A lot more is contained in neutrinos"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1291650,
    "dDurationMs": 2853,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and in photons of the\ncosmic microwave background."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1296870,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In 1972, Jacob Bekenstein proposed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1299750,
    "dDurationMs": 3670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "another source of entropy, black holes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1306260,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He suggested that the\nentropy of a black hole"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1308510,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "should be proportional\nto its surface area."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1311090,
    "dDurationMs": 4260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So as a black hole grows,\nits entropy increases."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1315350,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Famous physicists thought\nthe idea was nonsense"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1318410,
    "dDurationMs": 1410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and for good reason."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1319820,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "According to classical thermodynamics,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1321920,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if black holes have entropy,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1323600,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then they should also have a temperature."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1325970,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if they have temperatures,\nthey should emit radiation"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1329090,
    "dDurationMs": 2103,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and not be black after all."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1332750,
    "dDurationMs": 2910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The person who set out\nto prove Bekenstein wrong"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1335660,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was Stephen Hawking."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1337490,
    "dDurationMs": 3450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But to his surprise, his\nresults showed that black holes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1340940,
    "dDurationMs": 3930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "do emit radiation, now\nknown as Hawking radiation,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1344870,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they do have a temperature."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1347360,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The black hole at the\ncenter of the Milky Way"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1349340,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "has a temperature of about a\nhundred trillionth of a Kelvin,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1353240,
    "dDurationMs": 3030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "emitting radiation that\nis far too weak to detect."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1356270,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So still pretty black."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1358010,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But Hawking confirmed that\nblack holes have entropy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1360980,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and Bekenstein was right."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1363110,
    "dDurationMs": 3030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hawking was able to refine\nBekenstein's proposal"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1366140,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and determine just how\nmuch entropy they have."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1369230,
    "dDurationMs": 2730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The super massive black hole\nat the center of the Milky Way"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1371960,
    "dDurationMs": 4230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "has about 10 to the 91\nBoltzmann constants of entropy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1376190,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is 1,000 times as much"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1378260,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as the early observable universe,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1380330,
    "dDurationMs": 4050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and 10 times more than all\nthe other particles combined."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1384380,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that is just one black hole."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1386630,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All black holes together\naccount for 3 times 10"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1389870,
    "dDurationMs": 3123,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the 104 Boltzmann\nconstants worth of entropy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1394100,
    "dDurationMs": 3450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So almost all the entropy of the universe"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1397550,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is tied up in black holes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1399650,
    "dDurationMs": 1620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That means, the early universe"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1401270,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "only had about 0.000000000000003%\nof the entropy it has now."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1411590,
    "dDurationMs": 3660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the entropy was low,\nand everything that happens"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1415250,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the universe like\nplanetary systems forming,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1417770,
    "dDurationMs": 2730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "galaxies merging, asteroids crashing,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1420500,
    "dDurationMs": 3630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "stars dying, to life itself flourishing,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1424130,
    "dDurationMs": 2190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all of that can happen because the entropy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1426320,
    "dDurationMs": 3810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the universe was low\nand it has been increasing,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1430130,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it all happens only in one direction."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1432740,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We never see an asteroid uncrash"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1435380,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or a planetary system unmix"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1437450,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "into the cloud of dust\nand gas that made it up."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1440390,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There is a clear difference\nbetween going to the past"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1443270,
    "dDurationMs": 4230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the future, and that\ndifference comes from entropy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1447500,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The fact that we are going from unlikely"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1449810,
    "dDurationMs": 4893,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to more likely states is why\nthere is an arrow of time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1456830,
    "dDurationMs": 3390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is expected to\ncontinue until eventually,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1460220,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the energy gets spread out so completely"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1462800,
    "dDurationMs": 3630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that nothing interesting\nwill ever happen again."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1466430,
    "dDurationMs": 3510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is the heat death of the universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1469940,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the distant future,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1471140,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "more than 10 to the 100 years from now,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1473780,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "after the last black hole has evaporated,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1476270,
    "dDurationMs": 3990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the universe will be in\nits most probable state."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1480260,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, even on large scales,\nyou would not be able to tell"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1483260,
    "dDurationMs": 3570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the difference between time\nmoving forwards or backwards,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1486830,
    "dDurationMs": 3153,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the arrow of time\nitself would disappear."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1492980,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So it sounds like entropy\nis this awful thing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1495830,
    "dDurationMs": 1410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that leads us inevitably"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1497240,
    "dDurationMs": 2910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "towards the dullest outcome imaginable."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1500150,
    "dDurationMs": 3270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But just because maximum\nentropy has low complexity"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1503420,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "does not mean that low entropy\nhas maximum complexity."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1507020,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's actually more like this tea and milk."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1509840,
    "dDurationMs": 3030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean, holding it like this\nis not very interesting."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1512870,
    "dDurationMs": 4350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But as I pour the milk\nin, the two start to mix"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1517220,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and these beautiful patterns emerge."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1520220,
    "dDurationMs": 3330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They arise in an instant\nand before you know it,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1523550,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they're gone back to being featureless."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1526490,
    "dDurationMs": 3990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Both low and high entropy\nare low in complexity."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1530480,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's in the middle\nwhere complex structures"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1533330,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "appear and thrive."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1535250,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And since that's where we find ourselves,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1537590,
    "dDurationMs": 4023,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "let's make use of the low\nentropy we've got while we can."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1547610,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "With the right tools, we can\nunderstand just about anything,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1550550,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from a cup of tea cooling down"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1552380,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the evolution of the entire universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1554720,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if you're looking\nfor a free and easy way"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1556820,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to add powerful tools to your arsenal,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1559250,
    "dDurationMs": 840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then you should check out"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1560090,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this video sponsor, brilliant.org."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1562730,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "With Brilliant, you can master\nkey concepts in everything"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1565430,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from math and data science\nto programming and physics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1568550,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All you need to do is set your goal,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1570470,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and Brilliant will design the\nperfect learning path for you,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1573560,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "equipping you with all the\ntools you need to reach it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1576260,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Want to learn how to\nthink like a programmer?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1578180,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then Brilliant's latest\ncourse, \"Thinking in Code\""
    } ]
  }, {
